1
00:01:41,780 --> 00:01:49,009
[Genius Girlfriend]

2
00:01:49,600 --> 00:01:51,800
[Episode 12]

3
00:01:55,350 --> 00:01:56,479
Okay, class is over.

4
00:01:56,820 --> 00:01:58,160
[Reading Corner]

5
00:01:57,200 --> 00:01:58,729
Remember to revise at home.

6
00:02:01,900 --> 00:02:03,590
Class, don't rush off just yet.

7
00:02:03,590 --> 00:02:04,400
Director.

8
00:02:04,580 --> 00:02:06,920
[Reading Corner]

9
00:02:04,870 --> 00:02:06,870
I have good news to share.

10
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:08,840
Today, the school

11
00:02:08,840 --> 00:02:10,169
received an invitation

12
00:02:10,360 --> 00:02:12,750
to invite Lin Zhixia
from Class 1, Grade 10

13
00:02:13,030 --> 00:02:15,760
to attend the Marine Science Seminar
next month.

14
00:02:18,400 --> 00:02:19,910
The Marine Science Seminar

15
00:02:19,910 --> 00:02:21,410
offers tremendous value.

16
00:02:21,870 --> 00:02:24,910
Many experts and scholars in the field
will be there.

17
00:02:25,190 --> 00:02:26,430
Lin Zhixia's article

18
00:02:26,430 --> 00:02:27,760
has been chosen by them.

19
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:28,710
The organizer has

20
00:02:28,710 --> 00:02:30,280
asked her to share and exchange insights

21
00:02:30,280 --> 00:02:31,960
as a student representative.

22
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:33,430
This is the invitation.

23
00:02:33,430 --> 00:02:34,690
Lin Zhixia, come here.

24
00:02:35,470 --> 00:02:36,280
Class,

25
00:02:36,360 --> 00:02:38,020
let us encourage and cheer for

26
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:40,360
Lin Zhixia with our applause.

27
00:02:41,060 --> 00:02:42,220
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

28
00:02:46,750 --> 00:02:47,950
Thank you, Director.

29
00:02:48,310 --> 00:02:49,030
All the best.

30
00:02:49,030 --> 00:02:50,030
Class dismissed.

31
00:02:50,579 --> 00:02:53,290
[Invitation]

32
00:02:53,370 --> 00:02:56,130
Lin Zhixia, you are so energetic.

33
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:58,500
We had such a busy
school anniversary week,

34
00:02:58,500 --> 00:03:00,560
but you still had time
to do research.

35
00:03:00,810 --> 00:03:02,860
It's an old article
I previously published.

36
00:03:02,860 --> 00:03:04,590
I didn't expect it to be chosen.

37
00:03:04,650 --> 00:03:06,380
Lin Zhixia, congratulations.

38
00:03:06,970 --> 00:03:08,860
My mom always asked me
to go to this event.

39
00:03:08,860 --> 00:03:10,320
I'll go with you this year.

40
00:03:10,560 --> 00:03:11,560
You're going too?

41
00:03:11,640 --> 00:03:13,460
[Awards Board]

42
00:03:13,030 --> 00:03:13,400
Yeah.

43
00:03:13,870 --> 00:03:14,920
That's great.

44
00:03:15,030 --> 00:03:16,880
I was just feeling a little nervous.

45
00:03:16,880 --> 00:03:19,210
I've never presented at a seminar before.

46
00:03:19,340 --> 00:03:20,200
How about this?

47
00:03:20,290 --> 00:03:21,810
My mom's at the lab this weekend.

48
00:03:21,810 --> 00:03:23,270
You can ask her for advice.

49
00:03:23,690 --> 00:03:24,410
Okay.

50
00:03:25,020 --> 00:03:26,440
[Awards Board]

51
00:03:45,630 --> 00:03:46,340
Duan!

52
00:03:47,460 --> 00:03:48,660
Have a soda, my treat.

53
00:03:50,470 --> 00:03:50,900
Why?

54
00:03:52,690 --> 00:03:53,630
It's on me.

55
00:03:53,680 --> 00:03:54,740
Here, take it.

56
00:03:56,380 --> 00:03:57,380
Is it poisoned?

57
00:04:01,140 --> 00:04:03,350
Your side profile is amazing.

58
00:04:03,690 --> 00:04:05,020
Look at that jawline.

59
00:04:06,280 --> 00:04:07,210
Ma'am.

60
00:04:07,650 --> 00:04:09,410
Are you sick?

61
00:04:10,210 --> 00:04:11,740
Just tell me what you want.

62
00:04:14,620 --> 00:04:18,190
It's not a big deal.

63
00:04:18,740 --> 00:04:20,500
Well,

64
00:04:22,420 --> 00:04:25,420
I think the way you tossed the ball
the other day was...

65
00:04:25,910 --> 00:04:26,710
It was very...

66
00:04:27,100 --> 00:04:28,030
Get to the point.

67
00:04:29,180 --> 00:04:31,380
Can you get me a signed photo
of Han Geng?

68
00:04:31,930 --> 00:04:32,420
Why?

69
00:04:34,450 --> 00:04:36,659
Zhao Shuran from the next class

70
00:04:36,870 --> 00:04:38,400
insists that I got scammed.

71
00:04:38,690 --> 00:04:41,370
She said those who went to the concert
all got the signature.

72
00:04:41,370 --> 00:04:42,540
She was right.

73
00:04:42,870 --> 00:04:43,980
You were scammed.

74
00:04:43,980 --> 00:04:44,570
I...

75
00:04:47,330 --> 00:04:49,300
I don't want to lose face.

76
00:04:51,270 --> 00:04:52,620
Please help me.

77
00:04:53,010 --> 00:04:55,000
I have no choice.

78
00:04:55,250 --> 00:04:56,980
I'm willing to spend more money.

79
00:04:56,980 --> 00:04:58,010
I need it fast.

80
00:04:59,180 --> 00:04:59,740
Ma'am,

81
00:05:00,370 --> 00:05:02,130
with what money?

82
00:05:02,930 --> 00:05:05,250
Didn't you treat us to the amusement park

83
00:05:05,420 --> 00:05:07,280
with the money we got back for you?

84
00:05:08,130 --> 00:05:08,980
Yes...

85
00:05:09,420 --> 00:05:10,860
If I had enough money,

86
00:05:10,860 --> 00:05:12,520
would I be asking you for help?

87
00:05:13,010 --> 00:05:14,250
The Trendy Shop behind our school

88
00:05:14,250 --> 00:05:15,570
is selling Han Geng's signed photo

89
00:05:15,570 --> 00:05:16,570
for 800 per photo.

90
00:05:16,570 --> 00:05:17,810
Can I afford that?

91
00:05:21,420 --> 00:05:25,020
Duan, I know you have many connections
and tricks up your sleeve.

92
00:05:25,120 --> 00:05:27,210
I'm sure you can get me
a signed photo.

93
00:05:27,770 --> 00:05:28,500
Right?

94
00:05:31,660 --> 00:05:32,450
Please.

95
00:05:32,610 --> 00:05:33,690
Please...

96
00:05:34,130 --> 00:05:35,060
Please!

97
00:05:35,659 --> 00:05:36,659
Please...

98
00:05:36,980 --> 00:05:37,490
Stop,

99
00:05:37,510 --> 00:05:38,300
stop!

100
00:05:38,420 --> 00:05:39,220
Stop it.

101
00:05:41,740 --> 00:05:42,450
No.

102
00:05:42,690 --> 00:05:44,620
I think you're out of your mind.

103
00:05:44,860 --> 00:05:45,659
Duan Qiyan!

104
00:05:46,300 --> 00:05:47,830
Didn't I ask nicely enough?

105
00:05:48,370 --> 00:05:50,010
I used to think you were a loyal guy.

106
00:05:50,010 --> 00:05:51,500
Well, I was wrong.

107
00:05:51,690 --> 00:05:53,650
When you were young, you came to my house
and got beaten up by your dad.

108
00:05:53,650 --> 00:05:55,750
You even ate my food.
Did I ever complain about that?

109
00:05:55,750 --> 00:05:56,330
Also,

110
00:05:56,350 --> 00:05:58,010
once you left a bottle of tadpoles
at my place

111
00:05:58,010 --> 00:05:59,620
and they all turned into toads.

112
00:05:59,620 --> 00:06:01,420
It took me forever to catch them.

113
00:06:16,050 --> 00:06:18,050
If I lose out
in front of Zhao Shuran,

114
00:06:18,070 --> 00:06:19,730
I'll never go to school again.

115
00:06:19,770 --> 00:06:20,570
See you never.

116
00:06:23,130 --> 00:06:23,860
Wait.

117
00:06:29,860 --> 00:06:32,130
Now that's the Tang Tingting I know.

118
00:06:33,060 --> 00:06:34,190
That act just now...

119
00:06:34,420 --> 00:06:35,420
"Please..."

120
00:06:35,690 --> 00:06:37,090
Why were you acting cute?

121
00:06:40,370 --> 00:06:42,300
It's just an autograph.

122
00:06:43,250 --> 00:06:44,300
I'll help you.

123
00:06:45,740 --> 00:06:46,860
Duan!

124
00:06:47,500 --> 00:06:48,770
Hands off.

125
00:06:50,330 --> 00:06:51,130
Your treat.

126
00:06:54,860 --> 00:06:55,690
Class,

127
00:06:56,180 --> 00:06:57,440
today, we're studying

128
00:06:57,620 --> 00:06:59,610
[Constantly Strive to Become Stronger;
Strive to Be Number One]

129
00:06:57,890 --> 00:06:59,500
"My Castle in the Air."

130
00:07:00,190 --> 00:07:01,240
This prose

131
00:07:01,370 --> 00:07:03,250
adopts a writing style that combines

132
00:07:03,250 --> 00:07:04,980
both reality and imagination.

133
00:07:05,010 --> 00:07:08,370
The mountain cabin
is a real dwelling place.

134
00:07:08,400 --> 00:07:09,850
That's realism.

135
00:07:10,370 --> 00:07:12,350
It's also a spiritual resting place.

136
00:07:12,350 --> 00:07:14,010
That's imaginative writing.

137
00:07:14,840 --> 00:07:16,350
I'm so nervous.

138
00:07:16,930 --> 00:07:17,980
It's okay.

139
00:07:18,690 --> 00:07:19,690
I'm here with you.

140
00:07:36,430 --> 00:07:39,760
It symbolizes the balance
between materiality and ideals.

141
00:07:39,890 --> 00:07:40,620
Understand?

142
00:07:40,780 --> 00:07:43,440
What are you doing
instead of paying attention?

143
00:07:44,430 --> 00:07:45,470
Yes, you.

144
00:07:45,810 --> 00:07:46,540
Duan Qiyan.

145
00:07:49,220 --> 00:07:50,300
I've just explained

146
00:07:50,300 --> 00:07:51,930
the prose, "My Castle in the Air."

147
00:07:51,930 --> 00:07:53,130
Now, summarize for me

148
00:07:53,130 --> 00:07:55,040
the characteristics of the prose.

149
00:07:55,040 --> 00:07:56,040
What characteristics?

150
00:07:56,040 --> 00:07:56,800
This one.

151
00:07:56,830 --> 00:07:57,360
This one.

152
00:08:04,210 --> 00:08:05,940
[Han Geng]

153
00:08:11,620 --> 00:08:12,420
Duan Qiyan.

154
00:08:12,810 --> 00:08:14,070
What did I say just now?

155
00:08:23,780 --> 00:08:24,690
Duan Qiyan.

156
00:08:25,180 --> 00:08:27,370
I was wondering why you couldn't improve
your language test scores.

157
00:08:27,370 --> 00:08:29,430
So you're focused on this instead?

158
00:08:31,350 --> 00:08:32,679
What did you write here?

159
00:08:32,789 --> 00:08:33,320
Han Geng?

160
00:08:34,650 --> 00:08:35,380
Autograph?

161
00:08:36,460 --> 00:08:37,409
Seriously.

162
00:08:37,409 --> 00:08:38,120
Duan Qiyan,

163
00:08:38,500 --> 00:08:39,460
aren't you going to take
the college entrance exam?

164
00:08:39,460 --> 00:08:40,700
Are you planning to be a star?

165
00:08:40,700 --> 00:08:41,460
Are you?

166
00:08:41,940 --> 00:08:42,860
Is that it?

167
00:08:44,740 --> 00:08:45,530
Be quiet.

168
00:08:51,770 --> 00:08:52,770
Stop laughing.

169
00:08:53,820 --> 00:08:54,750
Let's continue.

170
00:09:09,580 --> 00:09:10,650
Tang Tingting.

171
00:09:11,050 --> 00:09:12,010
Long time no see.

172
00:09:12,170 --> 00:09:13,100
Have you been avoiding me?

173
00:09:13,100 --> 00:09:13,890
No.

174
00:09:14,740 --> 00:09:17,470
Haven't you brought Han Geng's
signed photo yet?

175
00:09:18,220 --> 00:09:19,770
I did.

176
00:09:19,860 --> 00:09:21,290
It's in the folder I keep

177
00:09:21,290 --> 00:09:23,150
in the bag drawer in my classroom.

178
00:09:23,890 --> 00:09:26,820
Liars tend to embellish details.

179
00:09:28,460 --> 00:09:29,660
You don't believe me?

180
00:09:29,940 --> 00:09:31,340
Follow me to the classroom, then.

181
00:09:31,340 --> 00:09:32,530
Okay, let's go.

182
00:09:32,580 --> 00:09:33,250
Let's go.

183
00:09:36,770 --> 00:09:37,500
Lesson time.

184
00:09:38,370 --> 00:09:39,970
I'll show it to you next time.

185
00:09:53,340 --> 00:09:54,050
Boss.

186
00:09:55,940 --> 00:09:57,980
I came to the store a while ago

187
00:09:57,980 --> 00:09:59,100
and asked about
Han Geng's signed photo.

188
00:09:59,100 --> 00:10:00,050
Do you remember?

189
00:10:01,460 --> 00:10:02,890
I remember. What's up?

190
00:10:04,890 --> 00:10:06,940
It's kind of embarrassing.

191
00:10:07,460 --> 00:10:09,820
I really want to buy that signed photo.

192
00:10:09,890 --> 00:10:11,410
Can you sell it to me first?

193
00:10:11,410 --> 00:10:13,700
I'll work part-time for you every day

194
00:10:13,700 --> 00:10:14,700
after school in return.

195
00:10:14,700 --> 00:10:16,050
The salary amount is up to you.

196
00:10:16,050 --> 00:10:16,770
Don't worry.

197
00:10:16,770 --> 00:10:17,890
I'm very eloquent.

198
00:10:17,940 --> 00:10:19,370
Hiring me is definitely worth it.

199
00:10:19,370 --> 00:10:20,370
I can see that.

200
00:10:20,500 --> 00:10:22,130
But you're too late.

201
00:10:22,700 --> 00:10:25,340
Han Geng's signed photo has been sold.

202
00:10:26,010 --> 00:10:27,100
Sold?

203
00:10:30,870 --> 00:10:31,530
Okay.

204
00:10:32,290 --> 00:10:33,170
Thank you.

205
00:10:33,500 --> 00:10:34,430
You're welcome.

206
00:10:49,240 --> 00:10:52,250
[New shoes in stock]

207
00:11:39,890 --> 00:11:40,650
How about this?

208
00:11:40,650 --> 00:11:42,450
My mom's at the lab this weekend.

209
00:11:42,580 --> 00:11:44,040
You can ask her for advice.

210
00:12:06,170 --> 00:12:06,980
Lin Zhixia.

211
00:12:10,970 --> 00:12:12,160
Why are you here?

212
00:12:13,150 --> 00:12:15,740
I remember you'd be at
Professor Shen's lab today.

213
00:12:15,740 --> 00:12:17,740
I happened to be in the neighborhood.

214
00:12:17,740 --> 00:12:18,580
It's raining.

215
00:12:18,600 --> 00:12:20,010
I thought you might not have an umbrella,

216
00:12:20,010 --> 00:12:21,340
so I stopped by to check.

217
00:12:22,050 --> 00:12:23,650
Thank you, my savior.

218
00:12:24,640 --> 00:12:25,170
Let's go.

219
00:12:43,370 --> 00:12:44,030
Lin Zhixia,

220
00:12:45,010 --> 00:12:46,620
what would you have done

221
00:12:47,290 --> 00:12:48,690
if I didn't come by today?

222
00:12:48,770 --> 00:12:49,940
Continue with my experiment

223
00:12:49,940 --> 00:12:51,740
and go home after the rain stops.

224
00:12:53,020 --> 00:12:54,620
What if the rain never stops?

225
00:12:57,220 --> 00:12:59,640
That's meteorologically impossible.

226
00:13:00,170 --> 00:13:02,800
The total amount of rain
on Earth is constant.

227
00:13:03,170 --> 00:13:05,030
After the rainwater evaporates,

228
00:13:05,290 --> 00:13:06,740
new clouds will form.

229
00:13:06,740 --> 00:13:08,340
It won't pile up infinitely.

230
00:13:08,950 --> 00:13:10,650
If it keeps raining,

231
00:13:10,740 --> 00:13:14,170
The atmospheric pressure will compress
these raindrops into fog.

232
00:13:14,170 --> 00:13:17,220
In the end, it will form a vast,
foggy state of chaos.

233
00:13:17,620 --> 00:13:19,020
Then we'd all drown in it.

234
00:13:19,700 --> 00:13:21,030
That's not what I meant.

235
00:13:21,860 --> 00:13:23,590
Then what are you referring to?

236
00:13:24,460 --> 00:13:25,340
I mean,

237
00:13:26,460 --> 00:13:27,650
if it keeps raining,

238
00:13:28,130 --> 00:13:30,130
and you have to ask someone for help.

239
00:13:30,860 --> 00:13:31,860
Who would you ask?

240
00:13:34,760 --> 00:13:35,380
Security.

241
00:13:35,410 --> 00:13:37,290
There should be an umbrella
in the security room.

242
00:13:37,290 --> 00:13:39,150
What if the security is not there?

243
00:13:39,390 --> 00:13:42,010
I'll ask my seniors in the lab for help.

244
00:13:42,700 --> 00:13:44,840
I'll walk them back to their dorms first,

245
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:46,840
and ask them to lend me the umbrella.

246
00:13:47,770 --> 00:13:49,500
What if they are all not around?

247
00:13:54,890 --> 00:13:57,150
I can't possibly let you come all this way

248
00:13:57,270 --> 00:13:58,800
just to pass me an umbrella.

249
00:14:02,500 --> 00:14:03,290
Right.

250
00:14:07,580 --> 00:14:09,640
Luckily, I happened to pass by today.

251
00:14:19,800 --> 00:14:27,420
♪ Wandering light wind
drifts past your pupils ♪

252
00:14:28,580 --> 00:14:32,900
♪ One second of encounter,
heartstrings stirred ♪

253
00:14:31,720 --> 00:14:32,980
Then I really am lucky.

254
00:14:33,430 --> 00:14:36,790
♪ The story feels altogether different ♪

255
00:14:39,000 --> 00:14:46,740
♪ How to describe
my whimsical wandering dream? ♪

256
00:14:47,990 --> 00:14:52,210
♪ You softly answer my quirky side ♪

257
00:14:52,600 --> 00:14:55,940
♪ Such bliss to finally be understood ♪

258
00:15:05,910 --> 00:15:07,510
And I called
Duan Qiyan's handwriting ugly...

259
00:15:07,510 --> 00:15:09,150
Mine is even worse.

260
00:15:10,620 --> 00:15:11,240
Tang!

261
00:15:18,030 --> 00:15:19,910
Tang, hurry up.

262
00:15:20,910 --> 00:15:22,570
Come down. What are you doing?

263
00:15:28,000 --> 00:15:30,120
Why are you looking for me at this hour?

264
00:15:30,120 --> 00:15:31,670
Do I need a reason to see you?

265
00:15:32,320 --> 00:15:34,650
Obviously, you have one. Get to the point.

266
00:15:37,630 --> 00:15:38,630
Actually,

267
00:15:39,750 --> 00:15:41,390
it's not a big deal.

268
00:15:42,390 --> 00:15:43,480
I just happen to have

269
00:15:43,480 --> 00:15:45,270
prepared a small gift for you.

270
00:15:46,150 --> 00:15:47,870
But I think it's more sincere to give

271
00:15:47,870 --> 00:15:48,840
gifts in person.

272
00:15:48,840 --> 00:15:50,360
So I came to you.

273
00:15:54,200 --> 00:15:55,080
Open it.

274
00:15:55,360 --> 00:15:57,360
What is it? So mysterious.

275
00:15:57,940 --> 00:15:59,290
Just open it up.

276
00:16:01,000 --> 00:16:01,870
Hurry up.

277
00:16:05,380 --> 00:16:07,810
[Han Geng]

278
00:16:06,630 --> 00:16:07,630
The signed photo!

279
00:16:08,150 --> 00:16:09,280
Where did you get it?

280
00:16:10,550 --> 00:16:12,630
Who do you think I am?

281
00:16:14,080 --> 00:16:15,510
This is

282
00:16:15,510 --> 00:16:17,600
a piece of cake to me.

283
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:20,550
Getting this signed photo

284
00:16:20,580 --> 00:16:23,600
is as easy for me
as getting full marks on an exam.

285
00:16:24,840 --> 00:16:26,150
Didn't you tell me

286
00:16:26,150 --> 00:16:28,010
you wanted Han Geng’s autograph?

287
00:16:28,650 --> 00:16:29,600
So I asked

288
00:16:29,600 --> 00:16:32,170
one of my many bros.

289
00:16:32,670 --> 00:16:34,270
He is part of the industry.

290
00:16:34,410 --> 00:16:36,030
He has some connections.

291
00:16:36,320 --> 00:16:37,270
I told him

292
00:16:37,270 --> 00:16:39,440
I wanted an autograph of Han Geng,

293
00:16:37,370 --> 00:16:43,370
[Han Geng]

294
00:16:39,790 --> 00:16:41,000
and he agreed.

295
00:16:41,000 --> 00:16:41,790
So,

296
00:16:41,790 --> 00:16:43,200
he asked Han Geng for it.

297
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:45,240
But there was a problem.

298
00:16:45,270 --> 00:16:46,470
What was the problem?

299
00:16:47,750 --> 00:16:49,630
Didn't you notice my shoes?

300
00:16:49,750 --> 00:16:52,770
These are the new shoes
I bought for this performance.

301
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:56,000
The shop owner of the Trendy Shop
behind our school

302
00:16:55,150 --> 00:16:59,820
[New shoes in stock]

303
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:57,750
raised his offer to 1,000 yuan

304
00:16:57,750 --> 00:16:58,670
to buy my shoes.

305
00:16:58,670 --> 00:17:00,000
But I declined it.

306
00:17:04,030 --> 00:17:05,400
But you know

307
00:17:05,720 --> 00:17:06,680
who Han Geng is.

308
00:17:06,680 --> 00:17:09,790
He's the hottest and best star now.

309
00:17:10,030 --> 00:17:11,750
Throughout the whole process,

310
00:17:11,750 --> 00:17:13,000
my execution

311
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:14,240
and calculation

312
00:17:15,920 --> 00:17:17,780
were nothing short of brilliant.

313
00:17:19,960 --> 00:17:21,880
Duan Qiyan, you big idiot!

314
00:17:32,900 --> 00:17:34,920
Shouldn't she be happy?

315
00:17:37,850 --> 00:17:39,310
Did I say something wrong?

316
00:17:44,240 --> 00:17:45,860
[A hundred-year undertaking
begins with education]

317
00:17:50,670 --> 00:17:54,420
[A New Chapter, A New Journey]

318
00:18:05,010 --> 00:18:05,870
Tang Tingting.

319
00:18:06,610 --> 00:18:07,850
So you knew that

320
00:18:07,850 --> 00:18:10,380
I sold my sneakers
to buy you the signed photo?

321
00:18:12,590 --> 00:18:14,390
Now that my sneakers are back...

322
00:18:14,850 --> 00:18:16,580
You returned the signed photo?

323
00:18:18,900 --> 00:18:21,210
How will you brag to Zhao Shuran now?

324
00:18:21,560 --> 00:18:22,400
Well...

325
00:18:22,900 --> 00:18:24,380
When did I brag?

326
00:18:25,050 --> 00:18:27,250
I'm an honest person, okay?

327
00:18:28,010 --> 00:18:30,290
Besides, no need for an overkill.

328
00:18:30,440 --> 00:18:31,610
I don't need a signed photo

329
00:18:31,610 --> 00:18:32,940
to outdo Zhao Shuran.

330
00:18:33,290 --> 00:18:34,180
You, on the other hand,

331
00:18:34,180 --> 00:18:36,050
act like you're soulless
without these shoes.

332
00:18:36,050 --> 00:18:37,780
Can you stop being so childish?

333
00:18:39,290 --> 00:18:40,980
Correction.

334
00:18:42,050 --> 00:18:43,310
These are not shoes.

335
00:18:45,250 --> 00:18:46,570
This is classic.

336
00:18:48,940 --> 00:18:50,140
Classic. Whatever.

337
00:18:50,480 --> 00:18:51,740
I've returned your stinky shoes.

338
00:18:51,740 --> 00:18:52,770
We're even now.

339
00:18:53,900 --> 00:18:54,570
Stinky.

340
00:18:56,440 --> 00:18:57,240
Does it smell?

341
00:19:01,440 --> 00:19:02,660
It doesn't.

342
00:19:06,660 --> 00:19:07,520
It smells good.

343
00:19:26,480 --> 00:19:27,440
Ms. Tang.

344
00:19:29,200 --> 00:19:30,260
Congratulations.

345
00:19:31,640 --> 00:19:32,880
I told you.

346
00:19:32,880 --> 00:19:34,880
Our class is full of hidden talents.

347
00:19:35,510 --> 00:19:36,750
Congrats to you, too.

348
00:19:36,960 --> 00:19:39,220
A participation award is still an award.

349
00:19:39,640 --> 00:19:40,920
Unfortunately, your class's award

350
00:19:40,920 --> 00:19:42,400
has nothing to do with you.

351
00:19:42,790 --> 00:19:44,720
All you did was clap on the side.

352
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:47,400
Do you know what a team is?

353
00:19:49,030 --> 00:19:49,890
Tang Tingting.

354
00:19:50,310 --> 00:19:52,720
You haven’t shown me
Han Geng’s signed photo yet.

355
00:19:52,720 --> 00:19:53,880
Are you going to say

356
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:55,310
